      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 46‑mile Ghost Town Trail now winds through Loop, marking the site with interpretive panels that tell the story of its coal‑mining past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://unitedstatesghosttowns.com/loop-pennsylvania-ghost-town/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "An underground coal fire erupted in 1962, forcing residents to leave and leaving a hazardous wasteland that still scars the landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://unitedstatesghosttowns.com/loop-pennsylvania-ghost-town/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Though abandoned, Loop’s remnants—mine gob piles and a coal‑washing plant—remain visible, offering a tangible glimpse into early 20th‑century mining life.",
